# Profile: eval-runner

Profile 1, the operator's example (ADR-0018; spec 002; ExecPlan 0005, Operation MP): run one eval set from the phone
or the Agent tab and report it. Only the Estate's reads and the eval and saved-flow actions are offered; one eval set
per request (profiles.PROFILE_REFUSALS holds the extra refusal in code).

`requires` is what a model must offer to wear it (STEW spec/profile.md 7a; ExecPlan 0006 P2): tool calling when it
offers tools. Its smallest context window is to be measured (the smallest window its cases pass with), not guessed:
until it is, `x-min_context` says so and `min_context` holds 1, which every binding meets, so nothing is checked for
it. Its reasoning effort is sent only when the binding offers the knob, so it does not require it.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "profile",
  "name": "eval-runner",
  "version": 1,
  "for": {
    "task": "run one eval set (or a saved eval flow) from the phone or the Agent tab, and say how a run did",
    "capabilities": ["A3", "C6", "N8"]
  },
  "tools": ["secondbrain_estate_status", "secondbrain_estate_logs", "secondbrain_approvals_history", "secondbrain_hold_status", "secondbrain_eval_status", "secondbrain_saved_flows", "secondbrain_saved_flow_status", "secondbrain_eval_start", "secondbrain_saved_flow_run"],
  "requires": {
    "tool_calling": true,
    "min_context": 1,
    "x-min_context": "to be measured",
    "reasoning_effort": false
  },
  "instructions": "One eval set per request: plan one eval_start with the set and the tag the request names, as your one step.\nA saved eval flow the request names is run with saved_flow_run instead, by its id from saved_flows.\nRead nothing else first: no code, no files, no skills.\nAfter the run starts, read eval_status once and say whether it began.\nAsked how a run did, read eval_status for its tag once, and give the pass count and each failed case.",
  "budgets": {
    "reads": 2
  },
  "reasoning": "low",
  "gates": {
    "bounds": ["keys", "archive", "untrusted-shell", "sitting", "whatsapp"],
    "extra": ["one eval set per request: a request for every set, or several at once, is refused in words"]
  },
  "card": "plan",
  "success": {
    "check": "tool_call_args_match"
  },
  "summary": "<set> <tag>: started, or <passed>/<total>, failed: <case ids>"
}
```
